{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChB1fxJTz1HQ37qfB7aQv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run test:ts` pass, and the Go build and `go test ./...` still pass.\n\nTicket 06 is done. Every checklist item is checked and committed, and all the gates pass: lint, typecheck, `npm run test:ts` (2089 passing), `go build ./...`, and the full `npm test`.\n\n**What I built** (all in `src/config/`):\n1. **`provider.ts`**: the built-in provider list, the lookups `lookupProvider` and `providerAt`, `defaultBaseURL`, and `sameEndpoint`. It also has one shared URL parser that treats `https:///v1` and `https:v1` as having no host, as Go does. `endpoint.ts` now uses that parser, so a config with an endpoint like `https:///v1` is now rejected when it loads, matching Go.\n2. **`family.ts`**: `inferFamily` and `canonicalFamily`. `load.ts` now imports `canonicalFamily` instead of keeping its own copy.\n3. **`credential.ts`**: resolves which API key a role gets, in this order: role variable, the profile's `api_key_env`, the provider's standard variable, then a stored key. It also has `overrideEndpoint` for the base-URL and protocol flags, which re-picks the key the same way. The `StoredCredentials` interface moved here from `load.ts`, which still re-exports it. Its `lookup` returns `{key, scope}` or `null`, as the ticket specifies.\n4. **`role.ts`**: `resolveRole`, `resolveFinderFlip`, `validateRole`, `validateEndpoint` and `isPlaceholderModel`. The role object itself is in `resolved-role.ts`, kept separate so `credential.ts` and `role.ts` don't import each other.\n\n**One thing callers need to know:** a resolved role is frozen, and its `apiKey` and store are hidden properties. That keeps the secret out of `JSON.stringify`, `util.inspect` and object spreads. The catch is that `{...role, model}` silently drops the key, so later code (the CLI's `--<role>-model` handling, for example) must use `updateRole(role, changes)`. I put this in `AGENTS.md`.\n\n**Testing:** all tests run directly against these modules, not through the CLI. The tests that check which `Authorization` header reaches the fake server need `review`, so they are left for ticket 20. Most resolution tests passed on their first run, so I broke the implementation deliberately to check they can fail. Four of the five breakages were caught. The fifth changed nothing, because the caller already makes the same check.\n\n**Not done:**\n- There is no debug tracing, because `@substrate-system/debug` doesn't pass the license check yet.\n- `isPlaceholderModel` sits in `role.ts` for now; the `init` starter ticket may want to move it.\n\nMy notes are in `.redeye/notes.md` (not committed)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":177,"cache_read_input_tokens":175606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":177},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"682f1424-ed5e-4ad8-82df-9c53c97a2745","uuid":"f95cce25-9c30-43c6-ba8a-7014718a460a","timestamp":"2026-11-18T20:19:15.744Z","request_id":"req_011ChB1fww9Po2uBSqXVXbAM"}
